  "text": " Never go shopping in fields and thickets. For clothes to wear like a coat or sweater. They have habits. They think much better when jackets get tight. They don't need mothers or fathers or brothers to get them. Mothers, they shed their pinchy old coats with vigor and grow another. And this one with vigor. Never.",
